' Paging a query across Task runs: what each page asks for, and whether another page follows.
'
' A paged load runs every page on a NEW Task node (see replaceTask in tasks.bs), so the node
' cannot be the memory of the query: each page must ask for exactly what the first page asked
' for. The screen holds the query as a plain AA and hands each run a copy with that page's
' startIndex. BaseGridView and the TV guide (Schedule) both page this way.
namespace paging

  ' The fields for one run of `query`, starting at `startIndex`. A copy: `query` itself is
  ' left untouched, so it stays the record of what every page of the load asks for.
  '
  ' @param query - the load's Task input fields, without startIndex
  ' @param startIndex - the first item to fetch
  ' @return Task input fields for this page
  function forPage(query as object, startIndex as integer) as object
    fields = {}
    fields.append(query)
    fields.startIndex = startIndex
    return fields
  end function

  ' Where the next page starts, or -1 when the load is complete.
  '
  ' A page that delivers nothing ends the load even when `total` says more exist: the next
  ' request would ask for the same startIndex and get the same empty answer, forever.
  '
  ' @param startIndex - the startIndex of the page just delivered
  ' @param delivered - how many items that page delivered
  ' @param total - the server's total for the query
  ' @return the next page's startIndex, or -1
  function nextStart(startIndex as integer, delivered as integer, total as integer) as integer
    if delivered <= 0 then return -1
    nextIndex = startIndex + delivered
    if nextIndex >= total then return -1
    return nextIndex
  end function

end namespace
